    "anchor": "Appendix D.1 bounded selfadjoint spectral calculus and unique nonnegative square root; ASTIS auxiliary real-L2 square-order corollary via Mathlib CFC monotonicity, consumed by B.15",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A4.SS1",
    "original_text": "Attributed mathematical restatement; exact selected boundary, with internally completed adapters.\nFor any measurable space Ω and any measure μ, let A and B be bounded real linear operators on real L²(μ). If A and B are positive (selfadjoint with nonnegative quadratic form) and B²−A² is positive, then B−A is positive. No finiteness or probability of μ, nontriviality, finite-dimensional L², commutation, or caller CFC instance is assumed. This is an ASTIS auxiliary consequence of positive square-root monotonicity, realized by the canonical complexification of real L²; it is consumed by the actual centered-root result.\nSource anchor: Appendix D.1 bounded selfadjoint spectral calculus and unique nonnegative square root; ASTIS auxiliary real-L2 square-order corollary via Mathlib CFC monotonicity, consumed by B.15",
    "text_sha256": "9ed471114b9b462c10faee2a1369fb98c6cca55fa4051af7bf8576402d52a4e4"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareOrder.positive_square_order",
